<title>SINGAPORE: IPCO in waterworks venture in Brazil.</title>
<headline>IPCO in waterworks venture in Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Infrastructure company IPCO International Ltd said on Thursday it formed a joint venture with two partners to develop the water and waste water sector in Brazil.</p>
<p>The US$40 million joint venture, Brazilian Water Works S.A. (BWW), had already identified several opportunities to begin work by year-end, IPC said in a statement.</p>
<p>The other partners in BWW are Anglian International, a subsidiary of Britain's fourth largest water company, Anglian Group Plc, and U.S.-based investment group Global Environment Fund, IPC said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
